I am aware of that. But I think the answer is more complete and useful if
one knows that you can indeed inadvertently land straight in her chamber
(and often bypassing Medusa is suggested when there are problems with the
titan or lacking means to pass the sea).

The basic principle is that there are always well defined points (stairs,
portals) or map regions defined where you will land, distinguished for the
direction (i.e. one point/region if you enter level from below, one if you
enter from above). This game behaviour is also effective in cases where e.g.
you are thrown back by the misterious force.

